    "<div style=\"font-family:'Gabriela', serif; color: #98cafcff; line-height:1.5;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "# What is an Array?\n",
    "\n",
    "An array is a data structure that stores a collection of elements of the **same type** under one variable name, making it easier to organize and manage data. Arrays keep code shorter and more manageable.\n",
    "\n",
    "Some programming languages allow arrays to hold only one type of data, while others—like Python’s lists and tuples—can hold different types. To change an element, assign a new value using its **index**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example: Tracking multiple students’ scores\n",
    "Instead of writing:\n",
    "\n",
    "`student1_score, student2_score, student3_score`\n",
    "\n",
    "Use an array:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "test_scores = [95, 88, 76, 92, 84]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Notice how the data is cleaner and all organized under the array test_scores.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Multi-dimensional arrays store more complex structures:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1cfaa559",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "```\n",
    "test_scores = [\n",
    "    [  # Layer 1\n",
    "        [95, 88],   # Row 1\n",
    "        [76, 92]    # Row 2\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    [  # Layer 2\n",
    "        [84, 90],   # Row 1\n",
    "        [78, 85]    # Row 2\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "]\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "608c262e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"font-family:'Gabriela', serif; color: #98cafcff; line-height:1.6;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "#### This example has 2 layers, 2 rows, and 1 column, forming a cube-like structure.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Arrays vs Tuples\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Arrays are mutable: their elements can be changed.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Tuples are immutable: their elements cannot be changed.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Tuples can contain mixed types, whereas arrays usually require uniform types.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Tuple Examples\n",
    "\n",
    "### Mixed Types:\n"
   ]
  },
